roke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Icing Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">powdered sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For sweetening and thickening the icing.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">meringue powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Or substitute with 1 egg white for stability.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2-3</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">water</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To achieve the right consistency.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">vanilla extract</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For added flavor.</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Optional Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">as needed</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">gel food coloring</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional for decorating.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-8935-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8935\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For combining ingredients.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Electric mixer&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For beating the icing.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">Piping Bags Piping Bags&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For decorating cookies.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8935-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-8935-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8935\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: In a mixing bowl, combine powdered sugar and meringue powder or egg white.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add water and vanilla extract gradually, beating on low speed until the icing is smooth.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Increase speed to medium and beat until stiff peaks form, about 3–5 minutes.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Divide icing into bowls and tint with gel food coloring if desired.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Transfer icing to piping bags and decorate cooled gingerbread cookies.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8935-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Let icing dry at room temperature for at least 2 hours before serving or stacking.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-8935-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>90</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>24g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here are the delightful ingredients needed to make your <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gingerbread\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gingerbread </a>cookies with royal icing!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for royal icing on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-8933\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups powdered sugar</strong> – for sweetening and thickening the icing</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons meringue powder</strong> – or substitute with 1 egg white for stability</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2–3 tablespoons water</strong> – to achieve the right consistency</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon vanilla extract</strong> – for added flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>gel food coloring</strong> – optional for decorating</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-gingerbread-cookies-royal-icing\"><strong>How to Make Gingerbread Cookies Royal Icing</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making Gingerbread cookies with royal icing is a delightful holiday tradition. The preparation time is about 20 minutes, with a cooking time of 10-12 minutes. Allow an extra 2 hours for the icing to dry before serving or stacking your <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookie\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cookies</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing-Preparation-Steps.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making gingerbread cookies royal icing, divided into four sections.\" class=\"wp-image-8934\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing-Preparation-Steps.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Gingerbread-Cookies-Royal-Icing-Preparation-Steps-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a mixing bowl, combine powdered sugar and meringue powder or egg white.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Liquid</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add water and vanilla extract gradually, beating on low speed until the icing is smooth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Beat for Stiff Peaks</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Increase speed to medium and beat until stiff peaks form, about 3–5 minutes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Tint the Icing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Divide icing into bowls and tint with gel food coloring if desired.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Decorate Cookies</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Transfer icing to piping bags and decorate cooled gingerbread cookies.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Let Icing Dry</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let icing dry at room temperature for at least 2 hours before serving or stacking.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>120 minutes (Icing Drying Time)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>152 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>24 servings</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Decorated and festive!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-gingerbread-cookies-royal-icing\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Gingerbread Cookies Royal Icing</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Chill your dough for at least an hour to make rolling easier.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a piping bag for precise royal icing application.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let your cookies cool completely before icing to prevent melting.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a touch of lemon juice to your icing for a delightful zing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different colors and designs for a festive touch!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-gingerbread-cookies-royal-icing\"><strong>How to Serve this Gingerbread cookies royal icing</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pair with a warm cup of spiced apple cider for a cozy treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a glass of creamy almond milk for a delightful contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Decorate a festive platter with assorted cookies for a holiday gathering.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a fun activity for kids by letting them decorate their own cookies.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Gift a box of beautifully decorated cookies to friends and family.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a scoop of vanilla ice cream for a delicious dessert twist.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Keep your gingerbread cookies and royal icing fresh with these simple storage tips:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Gingerbread cookies royal icing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow cookies to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place cookies in an airtight container with parchment paper between layers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store at room temperature for up to one week.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep royal icing in a sealed container to prevent hardening.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Gingerbread cookies royal icing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap cookies individually in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped cookies in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to three months for best quality.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Royal icing can be frozen in a piping bag; just thaw before use.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Gingerbread cookies royal icing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw cookies in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Warm cookies in a preheated oven at 300°F (150°C) for 5-10 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Avoid microwaving to maintain texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Decorate with fresh royal icing after reheating if needed.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How do you make royal icing for gingerbread?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make royal icing for gingerbread, you&#8217;ll need powdered sugar, egg whites (or meringue powder as a substitute), and a bit of water. Start by sifting the powdered sugar to remove any lumps. In a mixing bowl, combine the powdered sugar with the egg whites and mix on low speed until combined. Then, increase the speed and beat until the icing is glossy and holds stiff peaks. If you want a thinner consistency for flooding, add a little water until you reach your desired thickness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Which cookie is best for royal icing?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best cookies for royal icing are those that are sturdy and can hold their shape, such as gingerbread cookies or sugar cookies. Gingerbread cookies are particularly great because their spiced flavor complements the sweetness of the royal icing beautifully. Make sure to let your cookies cool completely before decorating to ensure the icing adheres well and doesn’t melt into the cookie.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the 10 second rule for royal icing?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The 10 second rule for royal icing refers to the time it takes for the icing to smooth out after being piped onto a cookie. If you drizzle a line of icing and it takes about 10 seconds for the surface to smooth back out, then the consistency is just right for flooding. This rule helps you achieve a nice, even layer of icing without any unsightly peaks or bumps.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Can you use royal icing for cookies?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Royal icing is perfect for decorating cookies. It dries hard, making it ideal for intricate designs and decorations. You can use it for outlining, flooding, and even creating detailed decorations. Just remember to let each layer dry completely before adding more icing or decorations to avoid smudging your beautiful designs.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As you dive into making these delightful Gingerbread Cookies with Royal Icing, remember the joy they bring! The aroma of spices and the sweet, colorful icing will fill your kitchen with warmth and nostalgia. Enjoy the simple pleasure of baking and decorating, and share these treats with loved ones. Happy baking!</p>\n",
